      "body": "## Overview\n\nOn CUDA, `quantization=\"mxfp4\"` failed MoE backend selection with a message that\nblamed the *deployment configuration* and listed only AMD-only candidates\n(AITER / amd-quark `EMULATION`), telling CUDA users to enable ROCm or install\n`amd-quark` — neither of which can help. The error now names the platform and\nstates that no usable MXFP4 MoE backend exists here. Fixes #61854.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The `select_mxfp4_moe_backend()` \"no backend\" error now names the platform\n  (`current_platform.device_type`) instead of implying the user's config is at\n  fault.\n- The per-backend rejection reasons are preserved, so the message stays\n  actionable.\n- No behavior change: the same configurations are still rejected; only the\n  message improves.\n\n## Validation\n\nCommands run (RTX 4090, CUDA, `.venv` editable install via\n`VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1`):\n\n- `python -m ruff check <file>` → All checks passed\n- `python -m ruff format --check <file>` → already formatted\n- module imports cleanly\n- Exercised the exhausted-backend path directly; it now raises\n  `quantization=\"mxfp4\" has no usable MoE backend on this platform (cuda) ...`\n  instead of the old \"supports the deployment configuration\" text.\n\nNo model-eval needed: this is an error-message-only change with no effect on\nmodel output, accuracy, or serving behavior.\n\n## Details\n\nWhen the platform has no native MXFP4 MoE kernel the candidate set is AMD-only\nby construction, so the previous lead sentence misattributed the cause and the\nlisted backends were unreachable. The reframed message keeps the candidate list\nand per-backend reasons but leads with the real situation and the platform name.\nScope is limited to the general `select_mxfp4_moe_backend()` path from the issue;\n`select_deepseek_v4_mxfp4_moe_backend()` carries the same wording and can follow\nup if desired.\n\n## Not duplicating an existing PR\n\nChecked `gh pr list --state open --search \"61854 in:body\"` and the mxfp4/MoE\narea: no open PR addresses this error-message issue. (#63349 refactors the MoE\noracle selection but does not change this message; happy to rebase on it.)\n\n## AI assistance\n\nAI assistance was used to author this change. The submitter reviewed every\nchanged line, understands and can defend it end-to-end, and ran the validation\ncommands above.\n",
